From e94314d34d6f2434db33a6b9ee3611cb84cb0da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 07:16:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-194: name the compose type in the tail banner - the
 receipt that stops a vacuous fidelity green

tail_compose's ct silently falls back to F32 when the body is not q4_0/q4_0. That is
the correct behaviour (only q4_0 has a quant->F16 pipeline; F16 over a q5_0 body
would push the whole compose onto the CPU) - but it meant NO LOG LINE distinguished
an F16 compose from a silent F32 fallback.

A fidelity row taken on an unnoticed fallback would reproduce the F32 numbers exactly
and read as 'F16 is lossless'. A vacuous green carrying a PLAUSIBLE number is strictly
worse than a skipped test: nothing looks wrong. This is the F-112 shape one level up,
at the feature layer instead of the test layer.

  KV precision tail ON - 1024 exact F16 cells ... body; compose=F16
  KV precision tail ON - ... ; compose=F32 (F16 REQUESTED BUT REFUSED: body is not q4_0/q4_0)

Every measurement run in the report now carries its own compose= receipt, verified
per run. A completed 6-pair decode A/B was DISCARDED and re-run because its runs
lacked -lv 99 and therefore lacked the receipt.

What this unblocked, both firsts:
- FIDELITY: at --temp 0 --seed 1, F32 compose and F16 compose generate CHARACTER-
  IDENTICAL text (90 tokens). tail-OFF diverges from both, which is the control
  proving the comparison is live. The lane is not a quality trade - this is the
  receipt for the source argument, not the argument.
- END TO END: until this run LLAMA_KV_TAIL_F16=1 had NEVER generated a token; every
  earlier probe OOM'd before serving. The four-site compose flip, the n_tail<=0 early
  return, F16 ggml_concat at real shapes and FA on F16 K/V are now all exercised.
- DECODE: +15.42% vs F32 compose, 95% CI [+10.94%, +19.90%], 8/8 ABBA pairs positive,
  t=8.14 df 7. Prefill unchanged (CI spans zero) = the attribution control lands: the
  compose runs per decode step, not in prefill.
- SCRATCH at the seat's real -b 512 -ub 256 (I had used defaults): 1358.57 -> 596.58
  MiB, -56.1%, from the real load pass's allocation bytes.
---
 src/llama-kv-cache.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
index 5ed2583835..08637e799c 100644
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
@@ -525,8 +525,19 @@ llama_kv_cache::llama_kv_cache(
                 LLAMA_LOG_WARN("%s: KV precision tail OFF - %s\n", __func__, refuse);
             } else if (want > 0) {
                 tail_n = want;
-                LLAMA_LOG_INFO("%s: KV precision tail ON - %u exact F16 cells per layer beside a %s/%s body\n",
-                        __func__, tail_n, ggml_type_name(layer_type_k), ggml_type_name(layer_type_v));
+                // lane-194: NAME THE COMPOSE TYPE. Without this there is no way to tell from a log
+                // which compose actually ran, and the F16 request silently falls back to F32 on a
+                // non-q4_0 body (llama_kv_tail_f16_compose / tail_compose's ct). A fidelity row taken
+                // on an unnoticed fallback would reproduce the F32 numbers exactly and read as
+                // "F16 is lossless" - a vacuous green carrying a PLAUSIBLE number, which is worse
+                // than a skipped test. Any F16 claim must quote this line.
+                const bool f16_req = llama_kv_tail_f16_compose();
+                const bool f16_eff = f16_req && layer_type_k == GGML_TYPE_Q4_0 && layer_type_v == GGML_TYPE_Q4_0;
+                LLAMA_LOG_INFO("%s: KV precision tail ON - %u exact F16 cells per layer beside a %s/%s body; "
+                        "compose=%s%s\n",
+                        __func__, tail_n, ggml_type_name(layer_type_k), ggml_type_name(layer_type_v),
+                        f16_eff ? "F16" : "F32",
+                        (f16_req && !f16_eff) ? " (F16 REQUESTED BUT REFUSED: body is not q4_0/q4_0)" : "");
             }
         }
 
